# Catalog file format

File: catalog/docs/catalog.oot

The public index is the file named `catalog` at the repo root.
opm fetches `https://catalog.openooda.org/catalog`. Each line is
one package version:

```
name|version|caps|deps|sha256
```

The line ends with a newline. `caps` is a comma list. Empty
`deps` is allowed. `sha256` is 64 lowercase hex digits of the
payload bytes.

`index` is a byte-for-byte copy of `catalog`. `index.minisig` is
the minisign signature of `catalog`. `registry.pub` is the public
key opm pins for the stock origin.

Example:

```
hello|0.1.0|FsRead||0e31868267f9f1baa1028cdeddade94266420d50a29ade6bb583090618bd97e2
echo|0.1.0|FsRead||8029d938971696a7e2903d368775356809ccf0fc121ac7f4dd24e46380d64fce
caps|0.1.0|FsRead||a063a691590961f65a7b257a19e0433559e339e9dab11b5e783565029abb794c
sqlite|0.1.0|||53a0406595a9ece3718f524fa02c0333bb34d53616d760c22958b5769cbbe616
```

Each child folder is one package. It holds `manifest` plus the
payload named in `payload=`. Academy headers are required on the
payload. Rebuild the index from the opm repo:

```
opm bot .
```

Run that with this tree as the target. Then re-sign `catalog`
to `index.minisig` with the catalog minisign key.
